#!/usr/bin/env python3
# mklang.py - makes amiga/lang_table.h, the words of Quill's interface in its languages.
#
# Each entry: the English as the C source writes it (C escapes, Latin-1: "R\351sum\351"), then
# German, French, Spanish and Italian (UTF-8, C escapes such as \n and \33c allowed; None: as the
# English). The translations must fit in Latin-1, the Amiga's character set.
#   python3 tools/mklang.py
#
# The work packages (docs/wordcraft-gap.md) keep their words in files of their own, tools/lang/wp<n>.py
# (each with a W list like the one below); their rows go into lang_table.h after the rows here, each
# package's between its own begin and end markers, so branches that add words merge cleanly.
